               <head>Liber sextus decretalium, with commentaries; England, 14th century, beginning and first half</head>
               <physDesc>
                           <p n="composite">Three parts, together early.</p>
                           <objectDesc form="codex">
                              <supportDesc material="perg">
                                 <support>parchment</support>
                                 
                                 <extent source="SC">i + <measure type="leaf" quantity="205">205</measure> leaves
                                    <dimensions type="leaf" unit="mm">
                                       <height quantity="385">c. 385</height>
                                       <width quantity="235">c. 235</width>
                                    </dimensions>
                                 </extent>
                                 
                             <!--    <condition>Imperfect and mutilated. The details of the missing leaves are in a handwritten catalogue in the Reading Room (see Bibliography below)
                                 </condition>
                                 -->
                              </supportDesc>
                              
                          
                           </objectDesc>
                           
                         <bindingDesc>
                            <binding when="1887"><p>Half morocco, 1887 (see Madan's handwritten description, which describes the earlier binding as 'marbled board side with leather back, 18th cent. ?'.)</p></binding>
                         </bindingDesc>
                           
                        </physDesc>
               
                        <history>
                          
                           <provenance>Three manuscripts together early as shown by uniform running heads added throughout (probably 14th century, second half). Parts A and C differ in script and layout but have very similar decoration. There are extensive annotations and marginalia, especially in parts B and C. </provenance>
                           <provenance>'285' (fol. 1r)</provenance>
                           <acquisition notBefore="1820" notAfter="1875">Acquired not later than <hi rend="italic">c</hi>. 1875</acquisition>
                           
                        </history>
