               <msPart xml:id="MS_Add_D_33-part1">
                  <msIdentifier>
                     <altIdentifier type="partial">
                        <idno type="part">MS. Add. D. 33 – Part A (fols. 1-85)</idno>
                     </altIdentifier>
                  </msIdentifier>
                  <msContents>
                  
                     <msItem class="#legalia" n="1" xml:id="MS_Add_D_33-part1-item1">
                        <locus>(fols. 1-85)</locus>
                        <author key="person_32352777">Guido de Baysio</author>
                        <title key="work_1903">Apparatus ad Sextum</title>
                        <note>Imperfect, with many missing and/or mutilated leaves: according to Madan's description two (?) leaves missing at beginning, one or more quires after fol. 22, one or more quires after fol. 34, a leaf after fol. 39, a leaf after fol. 68, four leaf after fol. 79. Fols. 40 and 69* are mutilated.</note>
                     <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  </msItem>
                  
               </msContents>
                  
                  <physDesc>
                     <objectDesc form="codex">
                        <supportDesc material="perg">
                           <support>parchment</support>
                           <collation mainStructures="12">Typically quires of 12; decorative catchwords; leaf signatures of more than one type, the fourth quire lettered 'v', the fifth 'x', etc.</collation>
                        </supportDesc>
                        <layoutDesc>
                           <layout columns="2" writtenLines="63">2 col. of 63 lines, ruled space <dimensions unit="mm" type="ruled">
                                 <height quantity="310">c. 310</height>
                                 <width quantity="180">c. 180</width>
                           </dimensions></layout>
                        </layoutDesc>
                     </objectDesc>
                     <decoDesc>
                        <decoNote type="border">Major decoration mostly lost, but a fragmentary border survives on fol. 69* recto. Not in Pächt and Alexander.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote type="flourInit">3- or 2-line blue initials flourished red.</decoNote>
                     </decoDesc>
                  </physDesc>
                  <history><origin>
                     <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notAfter="1350" notBefore="1300">14th century, first half</origDate>
                     <origPlace><country key="place_7002445">England</country></origPlace>
                  </origin></history>
               </msPart>
               
               <msPart xml:id="MS_Add_D_33-part2">
                  <msIdentifier>
                     <altIdentifier type="partial">
                        <idno type="part">MS. Add. D. 33 – Part B (fols. 86-160)</idno>
                     </altIdentifier>
                  </msIdentifier>
                  <msContents>
                     
                     <msItem class="#legalia" n="1" xml:id="MS_Add_D_33-part2-item1">
                        <locus>(fols. 86-160)</locus>
                        <title type="desc">Liber Sextus Decretalium with gloss of Johannes Andreae</title>
                       
                        
                        <msItem>
                           <author key="person_23416912">Boniface VIII</author>
                           <title key="work_1153">Liber sextus decretalium</title>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem>
                           <author key="person_24629057">Johannes Andreae</author>
                           <title key="work_2219">Apparatus ad Sextum</title>
                           
                        </msItem>
                        <note>Imperfect and mutilated. Madan noted one leaf missing after fol. 87, 24 leaves after fol. 96, one after fol. 121, one after fol. 138, 14 after fol. 150, all after fol. 160. Fols. 86, 126, 158, 159 mutilated.</note>
                        <note>Clement VI's bull 'Cum natura humana' of 1350 is added on fol. 153r.</note>
                        <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                     </msItem>
                     
                  </msContents>
                  
                  <physDesc>
                     <objectDesc form="codex">
                        <supportDesc material="perg">
                           <support>parchment</support>
                           <collation mainStructures="12">Typically quires of 12; leaf signatures partly survive (quires a-k)</collation>
                        </supportDesc>
                        <layoutDesc>
                           <layout columns="2" writtenLines="80">Textus inclusus, with the text surrounded by gloss, in variable proportionats; overall 2 cols. of c. 80 lines; ruled space <dimensions unit="mm" type="ruled">
                                 <height quantity="310">c. 310</height>
                                 <width quantity="185">c. 185</width>
                           </dimensions></layout>
                        </layoutDesc>
                     </objectDesc>
                     <decoDesc>
                        <decoNote type="flourInit">Penwork.</decoNote>
                     </decoDesc>
                  </physDesc>
                  
                  <history>
                     <origin>
                           <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notAfter="1310" notBefore="1300">14th century, early</origDate>
                           <origPlace><country key="place_7002445">England</country> (?)</origPlace>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance>Certainly in England at a very early date, as shown by marginalia.</provenance><provenance>
                        The name '<persName role="sgn" key="person_5112">Joshua Worrall</persName>' (18th century) is on fol. 160 (cf. MS. Rawl. liturg. e. 8)
                        

                     </provenance>
                  </history>
               </msPart>
               
               <msPart xml:id="MS_Add_D_33-part3">
                  <msIdentifier>
                     <altIdentifier type="partial">
                        <idno type="part">MS. Add. D. 33 – Part C (fols. 161-204)</idno>
                     </altIdentifier>
                  </msIdentifier>
                  <msContents>
                     
                     <msItem class="#legalia" n="1" xml:id="MS_Add_D_33-part3-item1">
                        <locus>(fols. 161-204)</locus>
                        <author key="person_148006">Johannes Monachus</author>
                        <title  key="work_6251">Apparatus in librum Sextum</title>
                        <note>Imperfect. Begins imperfect '-cia ut in simbolo atanasii' (VI.1.1, pr. Paris, 1535, fol. x), one leaf missing; another missing after fol. 186; ends  at 'interdicto ut in fonte-' (VI.5.11)</note>
                        <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                     </msItem>
                     
                  </msContents>
                  
                  <physDesc>
                     <objectDesc form="codex">
                        <supportDesc material="perg">
                           <support>parchment</support>
                           <collation mainStructures="8">Mostly quires of 8; leaf signatures in the usual form partly survive (quires a-f); catchwords.</collation>
                        </supportDesc>
                        <layoutDesc>
                           <layout columns="2" writtenLines="86"> 2 cols. of c. 86 lines; ruled space <dimensions unit="mm" type="ruled">
                                 <height quantity="325">c. 325</height>
                                 <width quantity="200">c. 200</width>
                           </dimensions></layout>
                        </layoutDesc>
                     </objectDesc>
                     <decoDesc>
                        <summary>Major decoration mostly lost: initials and borders survive on fols. 189v, 198r. Not in Pächt and Alexander.</summary>
                        <decoNote type="decInit">Initials.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote type="border">Borders.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote type="flourInit">3- or 2-line blue initials flourished red.</decoNote>
                     </decoDesc>
                  </physDesc>
                  <history><origin>
                        <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notAfter="1350" notBefore="1300">14th century, first half</origDate>
                        <origPlace><country key="place_7002445">England</country></origPlace>
                  </origin></history>
